// The Mosslight world: nine overworld rooms in a 3x3 grid plus a six-room dungeon. Geometry and
// doors were authored in phase 2; phase 3 added the first enemy spawns (see
// .autodev/phases/03-combat-enemies-determinism/PLAN.md). Phase 4 (see
// .autodev/phases/04-overworld-content/PLAN.md) makes the start room a cul-de-sac (its east/west
// doors and their reciprocals in south_shore/fallen_pines are removed), authors the sword, the
// lantern, three NPCs, the mill's step-plate puzzle, three secret chests off the main route, and
// the lantern-locked dungeon entrance. Phase 5 (see
// .autodev/phases/05-dungeon-puzzles-boss/PLAN.md) expands room.sanctuary_gate into a linear
// six-room dungeon (flooded_hall -> plate_chamber -> torch_vault -> warden_walk -> boss_arena),
// authors the beacon in room.lighthouse and both `SmallKey` doors. Every locked door is authored
// one-way (the reciprocal door carries no lock), matching the existing
// door.east_marsh.dungeon_entrance/door.sanctuary_gate.west pair — see DECISIONS.md. Chests, NPCs
// and torches carved into a room's own dead corridor never share the room's other decorative tiles
// (water at (2..3, 3..4), the interior wall at (6, 6), bush at (18..19, 11..12)), so every alcove
// below reuses the same (18..22, 1..2) pocket regardless of which room it is authored in.
World(
    version: 1,
    start: (room: "room.lighthouse", spawn: "spawn.lighthouse.start"),
    route: (ember_required: true, home: "room.lighthouse", goal: "room.boss_arena"),
    rooms: [
